Privacy Policy for LedgerPlus: Expat & Khata Book

Effective Date: 12 October 2026
Last Updated: 12 October 2026

1. Introduction

LedgerPlus: Expat & Khata Book (“LedgerPlus,” “we,” “our,” or “us”) is a personal finance application developed by Yuvraj Singh. This Privacy Policy explains how the application accesses, stores, uses, and protects information when you use our mobile application.

We are committed to protecting your privacy and providing transparency about our data practices.

2. Information We Collect and Store

LedgerPlus is designed to help users manage personal finances, income, expenses, budgets, and related financial records.

Depending on the features you use, information entered into the application may include:

Financial transactions, including income and expenses.
Budget information and transaction categories.
Currency preferences and application settings.
Other information you choose to enter into the application.

Local storage: If the application stores this information exclusively on your device, the information remains in the application's local storage and is not transmitted to our servers.

No account required: LedgerPlus does not require you to create an account to use its core features, provided that no optional account-based functionality is enabled.

We do not intentionally collect or transmit your personal financial information to our own servers. Any third-party services or software development kits integrated into the application will be disclosed and handled according to their actual data practices.

3. How We Use Information

Information stored within LedgerPlus is used to provide the application's features, including:

Recording and managing income and expenses.
Organizing financial transactions and categories.
Creating and managing budgets.
Displaying financial summaries, reports, analytics, and charts.
Saving application preferences, such as currency and theme settings.

We do not use locally stored financial records for advertising, marketing, or profiling.

4. Data Sharing and Disclosure

We do not sell users' personal financial information.

If financial information is stored exclusively on your device and no external transmission occurs, we do not share that information with our servers or third parties.

If you choose to export, back up, or share information using your device's available features, you control that action. The handling of information by the selected third-party service is governed by that service's own privacy policy.

Any additional third-party services integrated into LedgerPlus, if applicable, may process information as described in their respective disclosures.

5. Data Storage, Security, and Retention

Information stored locally by LedgerPlus is retained on your device for as long as it remains in the application's storage or until you delete it.

We take reasonable measures within the application's design to protect locally stored information. However, no method of electronic storage can be guaranteed to be completely secure.

You are responsible for maintaining the security of your device, including its screen lock and operating system updates.

If you uninstall the application or clear its storage, locally stored information may be permanently deleted. Exported files, backups, or copies saved elsewhere may remain until you delete them separately.

6. Data Deletion and User Control

You can manage the financial information you enter into LedgerPlus through the application's available features.

Where supported, deleting individual records removes them from the application's local storage. Clearing application data or uninstalling the application may also remove locally stored records.

Before clearing application data or uninstalling the application, consider exporting or backing up any records you wish to retain.

If future versions introduce accounts, cloud synchronization, or server-side storage, the applicable deletion procedures will be provided and this policy will be updated accordingly.

7. Third-Party Services

LedgerPlus may depend on third-party services or software libraries to support certain functionality. Such services may have their own privacy policies and data-handling practices.

Where third-party services collect or process user or device information, the relevant information, purposes, and recipients must be disclosed in this policy and in applicable Google Play disclosures.

Please refer to the privacy policies of relevant third-party providers for further details about their practices.

8. Children's Privacy

LedgerPlus is a general-purpose personal finance application and is not specifically directed at children under the age of 13.

We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe that personal information has been collected from a child in a manner inconsistent with this policy, please contact us so that we can investigate and take appropriate action.

9. Your Privacy Choices

You can choose what financial information to enter into LedgerPlus and can use the application's available features to manage or remove your records.

You may also choose whether to export or share information through other applications or services on your device.

10. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy when the application, its features, or applicable legal and platform requirements change.

Any revised policy will display an updated “Last Updated” date. Material changes will be communicated through appropriate means where required.

Your continued use of the application after an updated policy becomes effective is subject to the applicable policy and legal requirements.

